  "servings": 4,
  "summary": "This sweet Vietnamese dessert course features grilled <b>plantain skewers</b> wrapped in glutinous cassava dough and glazed with aromatic pandan honey. Ripe plantain sections are coated in a sweet coconut cassava paste before being thread onto bamboo skewers and caramelized over high flame. Charred grill marks add subtle smoky crispness that balances the lush tropical sweetness inside. A thick warm glaze made from pandan leaves, wildflower honey, and coconut cream is brushed liberally over the skewers as they roast. Toasted sesame seeds and crushed peanuts offer crunch, while fresh mint leaves and coconut flakes complete the vibrant plating. Served warm alongside lime wedges, this dessert skewer balances herbal sweetness, creamy fruit, and smoky char. Fast to prepare and visually stunning, it offers a memorable sweet finale rooted in classic Southeast Asian street flavor.",
